<title>UK: UK PSDR 36 mln stg in April.</title>
<headline>UK PSDR 36 mln stg in April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK public sector borrowing requirement data for April. Deficits unless noted (rep).</p>
<p> PSBR (in million stg)		 APRIL    MARCH	APRIL 96</p>
<p> Public sector			  36REP 8,917	 2,953</p>
<p> Central government		1,573REP 7,313	   607</p>
<p> Central government own acct   1,236REP 7,338	 2,582</p>
<p> Local Authority		   1,170	251	 1,474</p>
<p>   from central govt		 480REP    12REP	626REP</p>
<p> General Government		   77    7,576	 2,707</p>
<p> Public Corporation		   30    1,328	 1,103REP</p>
<p>   from central govt		 143	 13REP    1,349REP</p>
<p>NOTE - Forecast was 1.7 billion stg PSBR. Rep=repayment</p>
<p>GOVERNMENT RECEIPTS</p>
<p> Central govt total receipts  23,828     18,331    21,177</p>
<p> Inland Revenue receipts	 9,520	7,180     8,505</p>
<p>  of which income tax	    6,451	5,759     5,860</p>
<p>  corporation tax		  2,240	  467     2,272</p>
<p> Customs and excise		7,413	4,814     6,033</p>
<p>  of which VAT		     4,714	2,616     3,331</p>
<p> Social security		   4,699	3,761     4,210</p>
<p> Interest				703	1,593	 694</p>
<p> Other				 1,493	  983     1,735</p>
<p>CENTRAL GOVERNMENT OUTLAYS</p>
<p>   Total			     22,592    25,669    23,759</p>
<p>   of which Interest		1,677     1,917     1,600</p>
<p>   Net departmental outlays    21,087    23,997    22,237</p>
<p>NOTE- Privatisation proceeds in April were 172 million stg, compared with 78 million in April last year. The 172 million proceeds came from redemption of debentures of British energy.</p>
<p>The ONS said the 1996/97 PSBR excluding privatisation receipts was 27.55 billion stg, revised from 27.24 billion stg. In 1995/96, it was 34.12 billion stg.  </p>
<p>April's PSBR was reduced by 700 million stg from the second instalment of the Housing Corporation loan book and also by the second and final instalment of the sale of MOD married quarters which also raised 700 million stg.</p>
<p>Next month's PSBR figure may include privatisation proceeds from early receipts from the second call on Railtrack shares.</p>
</text>
